---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site';
---
<Base title={`Privacy | ${SITE.name}`} description="How Stayfile handles your files: they are processed in your browser and never uploaded." path="/privacy/">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">The files you open on {SITE.name} are processed by your own browser. They are not uploaded, stored or seen by anyone running this site.</p>
  <h2>Your files</h2>
  <p>Each tool reads your file into the memory of the browser tab, does its work there, and gives you the result as a download. When you close the tab, the data is gone. There is no account and nothing to sign in to.</p>
  <h2>What the site itself collects</h2>
  <p>The site is made of plain static pages. Like any website, it is served by a web host that may keep standard request logs, such as IP address and browser type.</p>
  <p>The site loads Google AdSense to show ads. Google may set and use its own cookies when it serves ads, and those are controlled by Google, not by this site. Files you open here are never part of that: they are read and changed in your own tab and are not sent to Google or anyone else. The site runs no analytics of its own and sets no cookies of its own.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this ever changes, for example if something else is added that could set a cookie, this page will be updated first. Your files will still never be uploaded.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy or the site: <a href="mailto:hello@stayfile.app">hello@stayfile.app</a>.</p>
</Base>
